     "text": "AGENDA MEMORANDUM\nBOARD: Board of Commissioners AGENDA ITEM #: 6.E.\nDATE SUBMITTED: November 13, 2024\nMEETING DATE: November 18, 2024\nFROM: Jose Pena, IT Director DEPARTMENT: IT\nDIRECTOR: Jose Pena\nAgenda Item: Consideration and action, if any, on the purchase of additional home\nequipment needed for Pharr Connect from Calix, Inc, through sole source proposal in\nan amount not to exceed $933,422.60. This item supports IF - Infrastructure.\nClassification: Regular\n(* If closed session, City Attorney must review and approve.)\nIssue: The City of Pharr uses Calix equipment for Pharr Connect services for our\nsubscribers. Due to increased demand for services, we need additional residential\nequipment to account for our projected growth this fiscal year. This equipment was\nbudgeted and we will work with Calix on a shipping schedule based on when\nequipment is needing to be received and used. We have included outdoor wifi access\npoints to deploy at city parks for the new smart town solution which will provide a better\nexperience to our subscribers and guest when visiting Pharr. Project No. 2425-01-518-\nP02-01\nFiscal Consideration: $933,422.60\nStaff Recommendation: Staff recommends approval of purchase.\nAlternatives: NA\nExclude Material from Public Packet? No\nReason: NA\nROUTING:\nJose Pena Created/Initiated - 11/13/2024\nMayra Gomez Approved - 11/13/2024\nHilda Pedraza Approved - 11/15/2024\nCynthia Garza Approved - 11/15/2024\nRicardo Rodriguez Approved - 11/15/2024\nJamison Merrick Approved - 11/15/2024\nCity Management Office Final Approval - 11/15/2024"
